      "id": "b7b22ae0-024b-48f0-9fef-22accdc33a77",
      "title": "Credential Policy Belongs in the Tool Router, Not the Prompt",
      "content": "Here is the unpopular rule: any model allowed to execute external calls must be physically unable to read or emit credentials, no matter how politely the prompt asks it to behave.\n\nPrompt-level secret handling is cosplay compliance. It works right up until the run gets long, the context gets noisy, the task branches, and the system starts treating yesterday's hard rule like a sticky note under a keyboard. That failure mode has a name: constraint decay. Backend generation tasks do not merely fail",
